Chapter: CoapPacketTest
  cites Encode chapter Coap

 Verify CoAP packet builders produce correct wire lengths, and the
 content-format constants their RFC 7252 registry values. The constants
 were the one assertion coap-encode carried that this test did not; its
 builder checks were list-length greater than zero, which is the
 blindness the CoAP interop story is about, so the exact lengths here
 are the stronger pin and coap-encode is folded in rather than kept.

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   let get = coap-get 1 [#AA] "temperature"
   in let post = coap-post 2 [#BB] "actuator" [1, 2, 3]
   in let ack = coap-ack 1
   in act
    print-line-uni ("GET len=" & show (list-length get))
    print-line-uni ("POST len=" & show (list-length post))
    print-line-uni ("ACK len=" & show (list-length ack))
    print-line-uni ("fmt text=" & show coap-format-text & " json=" & show coap-format-json & " cbor=" & show coap-format-cbor)
   end
  end

